# Trivy ignore file, read automatically by `trivy fs` and `trivy image`
# (CI: .github/workflows/reusable-upstream-image-scan.yml).
#
# This repo builds no image. The images it scans are the upstream ones the
# chart deploys (chart/values.yaml): postgres (image.*) and amazon/aws-cli
# (backup.awsCliImage). Their findings can only be fixed by moving the chart to
# a newer upstream tag/digest, so prefer that. Ignore only what cannot be fixed
# that way yet.
#
# Every entry needs, directly above it, a comment with:
#   - why it is acceptable (e.g. code path not reachable, fix not usable yet)
#   - the ticket that tracks removing the entry
# and an expiry date on the entry itself, so it is looked at again.
#
# No wildcards, no package-wide ignores, no entries without a CVE/GHSA id.

# postgres:15.20-alpine, usr/local/bin/gosu (Go stdlib v1.24.6). gosu is never
# executed by this chart: the image's entrypoint calls it only when started as
# root (`if [ "$(id -u)" = '0' ]`), and the chart enforces runAsNonRoot with
# runAsUser 999 on every container that uses this image (database and backup
# dump). Upstream does not rebuild gosu for stdlib CVEs. Go stdlib ids only;
# no other Go binary is in either image. OP-191
